<!-- Conclusion -->
<section id="sec-conclusion" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Use the Tangent Ratio With Confidence</h2>
  <p>Tangent is the ratio of the two legs: divide the opposite side by the adjacent side and you have described how many units of vertical rise come with each unit of horizontal run. The formula <span set:html={rich('[[\\tan(A)=a/b]]')} /> needs only two measurements, the answer is always a dimensionless number that can sit below, at, or above 1, and it grows as the reference angle grows. When a missing side is needed, <span set:html={rich('[[a=b\\tan(A)]]')} /> recovers the opposite side; when the angle is needed, <span set:html={rich('[[A=\\tan^{-1}(a/b)]]')} /> recovers it. Ramp, roof, ladder, or textbook 3-4-5, the method never changes: identify the opposite side, identify the adjacent side, divide, and verify with the positive-ratio check.</p>
</section>
